              1  * ============================================================
              2  * VGM Player for TMS9900 by Paul Chernikhowsky
              3  * Assembler: asm990
              4  *
              5  * Plays back a VGM format file using the YM3812 FM synthesis ch
              6  *
              7  * Note that hex constants in this file use the TMS 9900 format 
              8  * 
              9  * Code origin: 0x8000 (code must be loaded at this RAM location
             10  * VGM data:    0x9000 (VGM data file must be located starting a
             11  *
             12  * YM3812 CRU mapping:
             13  *   CRU bits 0-7 = D0-D7  (data bus, 8 bits)
             14  *   CRU bit  8   = A0     (0=address write, 1=data write)
             15  *   CRU bit  9   = /CS    (chip select, active low)
             16  *   CRU bit  A   = /RD    (read strobe,  active low)
             17  *   CRU bit  B   = /WR    (write strobe, active low)
             18  *
             19  * Register usage:
             20  *   R0  - scratch / CRU data byte
             21  *   R1  - VGM program counter (byte address)
             22  *   R2  - current VGM command byte
             23  *   R3  - YM3812 register address (for OPL write)
             24  *   R4  - YM3812 data byte (for OPL write)
             25  *   R5  - wait sample count (16-bit)
             26  *   R6  - scratch / loop counter
             27  *   R7  - scratch
             28  *   R8  - VGM loop point address (0 = no loop)
             29  *   R14 - saved PC
             30  *   R15 - saved ST
             31  *
             32  * ============================================================
             33  
